{"id":"vectorbloom","title":"Vectorbloom","url":"https://aesthetics.fandom.com/wiki/Vectorbloom","rev":239568,"fetched":"2026-10-16","lead":[{"t":"p","c":[{"t":"b","c":["Vectorbloom"]}," is an aesthetic that rose to popularity during the early 2000s until the early 2010s. The aesthetic was characterized by the era's fascination with digital graphic vector tools and applying their capabilities to create complex, fantastical and psychedelic manipulations of natural forms. It draws inspiration from the graphic styles of 1960s ",{"t":"a","c":["Psychedelia"],"href":"https://aesthetics.fandom.com/wiki/Psychedelia"},", 1970s ",{"t":"a","c":["Supergraphic Ultramodern"],"id":"supergraphic-ultramodern"},", and the organic curves of ",{"t":"a","c":["Art Nouveau"],"id":"art-nouveau"},"."]},{"t":"p","c":["Vectorbloom coexisted alongside ",{"t":"a","c":["Frutiger Aero"],"id":"frutiger-aero"}," and ",{"t":"a","c":["Vectordelia"],"id":"vectordelia"},", but distinguished itself through its reliance on highly intricate, maximalist patterns, often containing flat colors and dramatic gradients. The style is closely related to the ",{"t":"a","c":["McBling"],"href":"https://aesthetics.fandom.com/wiki/McBling"}," and \"",{"t":"a","c":["2000s Baroque"],"id":"2000s-modern-baroque"},"\" aesthetics, emphasizing technological opulence and visual density."]}],"sections":[{"title":"Visuals","id":"visuals","blocks":[{"t":"p","c":["Common characteristics of Vectorbloom are based around the maximalist use of vector-based elements, including flowers, elaborate flourishes, and occasionally abstract animals or hybrid water creatures. These patterns are designed using digital graphic tools, enabling designers to manipulate images and forms into an intricate, \"blooming\" like pattern. The aesthetic is usually executed on exclusively flat surfaces, though occasional design work utilizes pseudo-3D effects."]},{"t":"p","c":["Vectorbloom designs are prominent in commercial and architectural spaces, often demonstrating a new form of interactivity through graphic design. Katrin Olina, an Icelandic graphic artist, pioneered this visual language in interiors, creating fantastical worlds of multilayered imagery. Her work on Hong Kong's Cristal Bar involved creating a single, seamless image that acted as an inner lining, welding four interconnected spaces together. The graphics spread across every wall, ceiling, and floor, morphing in color and pattern to transform the environment. This visual strategy was also noted in the late 2000s design trend of \"frozen yogurt futurism,\" exemplified by retail locations like SNOG Frozen Yogurt."]}]},{"title":"Music","id":"music","blocks":[{"t":"h","l":3,"c":["Songs"]},{"t":"ul","items":[{"c":[{"t":"a","c":["PinkPantheress - Turn it up"],"href":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=HC5oBBQg9q8"}]},{"c":[{"t":"a","c":["Samantha James - Rise"],"href":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VGCVMs9InL4&list=PLUvsk07hdBM1pkZmX0WjKhcazRyiYe2c7"}]},{"c":[{"t":"a","c":["otetsu - Black Gold (feat. Megurine Luka)"],"href":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0ozfkoVdvLY"}]},{"c":[{"t":"a","c":["Dame De Lotus - Emilie Simon"],"href":"https://youtu.be/N2odfjNMZVQ"}]},{"c":[{"t":"a","c":["Headlock - Imogen Heap"],"href":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=IXdIxKQ-qWQ"}]},{"c":[{"t":"a","c":["Hachiouji & kz (livetune) - Weekender Girl (feat. Hatsune Miku)"],"href":"https://m.youtube.com/watch?v=06d8SwcSm_Q&feature=youtu.be"}," (VG)"]},{"c":[{"t":"a","c":["Freetempo - Harmony"],"href":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=l_EvrwQPUG0"}]},{"c":[{"t":"a","c":["Reni Jusis - Motyle"],"href":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=NiTyf-Jy04o"}]}]}]},{"title":"Media","id":"media","blocks":[{"t":"h","l":3,"c":["Video Games"]},{"t":"ul","items":[{"c":[{"t":"i","c":["Lumines"]}," (2004)"]},{"c":[{"t":"i","c":["Feel the Magic: XY/XX"]}," (2004)"]},{"c":[{"t":"i","c":["The Rub Rabbits"]}," (2005)"]},{"c":[{"t":"i","c":["PixelJunk Eden"]}," (2008)"]},{"c":[{"t":"i","c":["Child of Eden"]}," (2011)"]},{"c":[{"t":"i","c":["Ibb & Obb"]}," (2013)"]},{"c":[{"t":"i","c":["Hohokum"]}," (2014)"]},{"c":[{"t":"i","c":["Tetris The Grand Master 4 Absolute Eye"]}," (2025)"]}]},{"t":"h","l":3,"c":["TV Shows"]},{"t":"ul","items":[{"c":[{"t":"i","c":["Pimp My Ride"]}," (2005)"]},{"c":[{"t":"i","c":["Ayakashi: Samurai Horror Tales"]}," (2006)"]},{"c":[{"t":"i","c":["Mononoke"]}," (2007)"]},{"c":[{"t":"i","c":["Stoked"]}," (2009-2013)"]},{"c":[{"t":"i","c":["Ever After High"]}," (2013-2018)"]}]}]},{"title":"Resources","id":"resources","blocks":[{"t":"ul","items":[{"c":[{"t":"a","c":["https://web.archive.org/web/20221118081745/https://twitter.com/y2k_aesthetic/status/1554350229733789696"],"href":"https://web.archive.org/web/20221118081745/https://twitter.com/y2k_aesthetic/status/1554350229733789696"}]},{"c":[{"t":"a","c":["https://www.dezeen.com/2008/10/19/new-installations-by-katrin-olina/"],"href":"https://www.dezeen.com/2008/10/19/new-installations-by-katrin-olina/"}]},{"c":[{"t":"a","c":["https://katrinolina.com/project/cristal-bar"],"href":"https://katrinolina.com/project/cristal-bar"}]}]}]},{"title":"Gallery","id":"gallery","blocks":[{"t":"gallery","items":[{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/c/ca/Original_e5af7f81ade009c05c42a44ea974f972.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20221119162407","w":150,"h":150},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/1/15/Original_cf01f700805573b10f49b1a1dadc5062.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20221119162329","w":150,"h":150},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/9/9a/Original_3891a203d721d4e8ccb09582a87a4c00.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20221120001214","w":150,"h":150},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/e/eb/Original_88c16fff646fef2996003561108d89f3.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20221120004602","w":150,"h":150},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/4/4f/Original_f3f1078bdbbe6689e068d242600877a8.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20221120011918","w":150,"h":150},{"src":